00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.590
Apparently it was a 30 minute phone call and
we only got 10 minutes in the summary.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:35.309
Yes, so this is, I've been repeating this
time and again and it's important to nice

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:38.159
that you understand it, but we need more people
to understand it.

00:00:38.159 --> 00:00:43.570
Donald Trump teased the release of the transcript
of the July 25 phone call.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.019
When we got that, it obviously wasn't a transcript.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:49.249
It was a very partial transcripts transcript.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:56.159
We can't even call it a summary because a
summary would in in sort of a narrative form

00:00:56.159 --> 00:00:59.140
tell the story of everything that was said
in the phone call.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.769
All they did is take a couple pieces of the
transcript.

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:04.449
The call is known to have been a half hour
phone call.

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:08.100
I think you're being generous when you say
the transcript covers about 10 minutes.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.490
It might only cover six, seven or eight minutes.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:16.000
By my estimation, Donald Trump has continued
to say, I have released the transcript and

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.780
it was a perfect phone call.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:22.409
And the most disgusting and disturbing thing
about this is if you look at, we have a call

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:28.640
up on our YouTube channel from last week's
show, it's called something like furious Trumpist

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.640
implode spectacularly.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.320
You know, we came up with some interesting
title on YouTube, but one of the things that

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.030
this person said during their call to me when
they went from one allegation to another,

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.229
it didn't, it was just circular.

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:43.909
They eventually said, listen, we saw the whole
transcript and it's fine.

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:47.030
And I had to remind him, we didn't see the
whole transcript.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:51.340
We saw what our six to eight minutes of the
transcript, it was a 30 minute phone call

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.000
and you have fallen for the completely fake
narrative that the transcript is out there.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.359
So are we ever going to see the full transcript?

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:01.359
I don't know.

00:02:01.359 --> 00:02:05.359
Uh, if we put more pressure on and talk about
it, are we going to see it?

00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:06.420
I, I'm not sure.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.659
We've put more pressure on seeing Trump's
tax returns.

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:15.450
And I guess we could say we're slightly closer
to maybe someday seeing some version of them,

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.819
but it hasn't really done much so far.

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:20.400
So you know, there, there is scandal fatigue.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.940
There are also so many different elements
to this thing.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:28.310
There is, you've got the Devin newness, uh,
as a co-conspirator, uh, traveling to Vienna

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.190
to meet with Victor Shoken on taxpayer dollars.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:36.030
You've got Donald Trump blurting out on Fox
and friends over the weekend that, Oh yeah,

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.630
actually, uh, I did ask them to do, to look
into this and why should we be giving them

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:45.340
hundreds of millions of dollars anyway, linking
for the first time, the quote investigation

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.340
and the money.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:52.580
My point is there's so many elements of this
that it can be hard to get refocused on any

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:56.209
one thing even when we've obviously been lied
